<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<PermissionSet xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        2026-09-03, M5 legacy Task retirement (agent-output/design-legacy-task-retirement.md §5 Step 4,
        both waves shipped together per an explicit user waiver of the cutover rollback window).
        STRIPPED 12 of 16 fieldPermissions blocks — the 6 retiring field names (Task_Group__c,
        Transaction_Deal__c, Verbal_Verification_Completed__c, Verified_By__c, Verified_At__c,
        Verification_Phone__c) on BOTH Task.* and Event.*.
        KEPT Task_Owner_Label__c AND Task_Sequence__c on BOTH Task and Event — both are Property
        Management fields (OnboardingFanoutService.cls writes both; OnboardingController.cls renders
        the Owner column from Task_Owner_Label__c).
        🔴 TWO CORRECTIONS TO THE DESIGN, FOUND BY RETRIEVING THE ORG COPY BEFORE EDITING (mandatory
        per this repo's "PermissionSet deploy REPLACES its whole fieldPermissions block" rule):
        (1) The design's admin prompt (§9) said to keep only Task_Owner_Label__c; it did not flag that
        Task_Sequence__c is present in this same file and is equally one of the three PM-survivor
        fields (design §2.2) — both are retained.
        (2) 🔴 THE ORG COPY OF THIS FILE CARRIED AN ENTIRE Event.* BLOCK (8 fieldPermissions) THAT DID
        NOT EXIST IN THIS REPO FILE AT HEAD AT ALL — repo had 8 Task.* rows only, org had those same 8
        Task.* rows PLUS 8 parallel Event.* rows (retrieved+diffed 2026-09-03, usman-dpeg). Shipping
        the HEAD-only 8-field version would have been accepted as a "complete file" and would have
        SILENTLY REVOKED all 8 org Event.* grants on deploy, including the two survivor fields,
        exactly the failure mode this repo's standing PermissionSet warning describes. This file is
        now a true superset of both HEAD and the org copy, less the 12 retired blocks.
        Per P8 (Tooling query against usman-dpeg, 2026-09-03), this permission set currently has ZERO
        PermissionSetAssignment rows — relevant to OQ-M5-4 (whether it could be retired wholesale) but
        amended, not deleted, per the design's default and this change's explicit scope.
    -->
    <description>Read-only FLS on the custom Activity fields the Transaction and Onboarding checklists read; a shared building block for personas that VIEW a checklist without working it. DPEG_Task_Edit remains the read/write counterpart for personas that complete tasks.</description>
    <fieldPermissions>
        <editable>false</editable>
        <field>Event.Task_Owner_Label__c</field>
        <readable>true</readable>
    </fieldPermissions>
    <fieldPermissions>
        <editable>false</editable>
        <field>Event.Task_Sequence__c</field>
        <readable>true</readable>
    </fieldPermissions>
    <fieldPermissions>
        <editable>false</editable>
        <field>Task.Task_Owner_Label__c</field>
        <readable>true</readable>
    </fieldPermissions>
    <fieldPermissions>
        <editable>false</editable>
        <field>Task.Task_Sequence__c</field>
        <readable>true</readable>
    </fieldPermissions>
    <hasActivationRequired>false</hasActivationRequired>
    <label>Task Checklist – View Only</label>
</PermissionSet>
